  the US market (spec §8), and every <url> below repeats the full alternate set
  because Google requires the annotation to be reciprocal on every URL.

  /dev-zone is deliberately absent: it is a client-only whiteboard route that
  scripts/prerender.js does not snapshot, so it would resolve to an empty shell
  for any crawler that followed it.

  No <lastmod>: a guessed date is worse than none, and Google ignores the field
  when it cannot be trusted.
-->
